<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1633" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">agrĭcultūra</span></b> ,
		ae, f., better separately, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">agri cultūra</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>agriculture.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">insitiones, quibus nihil invenit agri
					culturā sollertius,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Sen. 15</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id.
				Off. 1, 42</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">agri culturae studere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. G. 6, 22</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">homo agri culturae deditus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					2 Par. 26, 10</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b> (eccl. Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Dei agri cultura estis,</span>”
				<i>God's husbandry</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. 1
					Cor. 3, 9</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
